{
 "clause": "CG-10",
 "document": "10-claim-gated-admission.md",
 "version": 3,
 "also": [
  "CG-9"
 ],
 "operation": "claim_ticket",
 "distinguishes": "Which frame carries a transaction's ticket: the first VERIFY frame to a ticket paymaster the node accepts at its head, whose 168 bytes of data are the epoch, the salt and the signature, with the paymaster's key as the issuer. A node that takes a ticket from a DEFAULT frame, from a paymaster it does not accept, from the last ticket frame rather than the first, checks it against every key it accepts rather than the paymaster's, or reads data of another length, fails here.",
 "provenance": "Every signature comes from Commonware at c18a6b9 (cryptography's ops::sign_message, and ops::sign for the cases signed without a namespace, for MinSig), run as a program outside this repository, each valid one also issued blind there and found equal; its points are written here in EIP-2537's encoding. Each case's verdict on a well-formed ticket was confirmed by the Hegota testnet's EIP-2537 pairing precompile; which frame is read is by hand from CG-10. The last case is a spend the testnet mined (exp-frames f0749cb), with its paymaster and its issuers' key: read as a ticket, and not valid, since it was signed under that run's namespace.",
